      "boundElements": [],
      "updated": 1772502236124,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "- Standardize all units, ratings, serving\nquantities, etc.\n\n- normalize the names and vectorize the\ningredients and its quantity values \n  \n- Instruction tokenization or standardize into\nvectors, list so we can put it to models easier\n\n- Handling missing values (nutrients, kcal of\nmeals) if any, using nutrient dataset. This\nimportant for diet matching and health score\ncalculation\n\n- Normalize the rating between different sub-\ndatasets\n\n- Create image naming syntax for storage\n\n- Create different tagging category features,\nsuch as Dietary/Nutrient, Cuisine/Flavor, Meal\nType using the ingredients. Or use which\ndatasets that have these tagging then train a\nclassification model to apply to the remaining\nrecords)\n\n- remove near duplicate recipes using shingling\n\n- Calculate health score of recipes\n...",
      "fontSize": 26.2916798942023,
      "fontFamily": 5,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": "e6fl33hjPArnwDVdCQV7d",
      "originalText": "- Standardize all units, ratings, serving quantities, etc.\n\n- normalize the names and vectorize the ingredients and its quantity values \n  \n- Instruction tokenization or standardize into vectors, list so we can put it to models easier\n\n- Handling missing values (nutrients, kcal of meals) if any, using nutrient dataset. This important for diet matching and health score calculation\n\n- Normalize the rating between different sub-datasets\n\n- Create image naming syntax for storage\n\n- Create different tagging category features, such as Dietary/Nutrient, Cuisine/Flavor, Meal Type using the ingredients. Or use which datasets that have these tagging then train a classification model to apply to the remaining records)\n\n- remove near duplicate recipes using shingling\n\n- Calculate health score of recipes\n...",
      "autoResize": true,
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    },
