    {
      "id": "K2yrzPMA2h2haHabSFubY",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 8272.291520370069,
      "y": -4457.431558215432,
      "width": 977.3038330078125,
      "height": 887.3441964293276,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#1e1e1e",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 2,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 1,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "index": "b2k",
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 493372239,
      "version": 5026,
      "versionNonce": 983155144,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": [],
      "updated": 1772502236124,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "\n- Functional,Flavor & Structural Analysis. Explore ingredient role in a meal\nand how to classify them. This can help us later when doing substitution. \n\n- Explore how to create different tagging category features, such as\nDietary/Nutrient, Cuisine/Flavor, Meal Type using the ingredients. Or use\nwhich datasets that have these tagging then train a classification model\nto apply to the remaining records)\n\n- Co-occurence/ item sets analysis to find out core ingredients, flavor\ningredients, etc. Also, creating an ingredient network so we have an\nunderstanding of central nodes (ingredients which are hard to be replaced)\nand what they are usually being used with. \n\n\n- Complements & Substitution analysis to find how we can switch\ningredients for a certain recipe, or can we add in certain extra ingredients.\nWe can try different options such as reading reviews for keyword such as 'I\nuse X instead of Y', 'I subtitute A with B', etc. then build Substitution\nNetworks. Or doing Ingredient Embedding Analysis (maybe using Word2Vec\ntrained on out dataset or something else). Cluster analysis would also be\ninteresting, ingredient in a group are more likely to be used as substitute\n\n- Explore PCA of recipe-ingredient matrix might yield insights on how these\ningredients are used together.\n\n...",
      "fontSize": 26.2916798942023,
      "fontFamily": 5,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": "KI5kqy3pRmhAqUPls2DbN",
      "originalText": "\n- Functional,Flavor & Structural Analysis. Explore ingredient role in a meal and how to classify them. This can help us later when doing substitution. \n\n- Explore how to create different tagging category features, such as Dietary/Nutrient, Cuisine/Flavor, Meal Type using the ingredients. Or use which datasets that have these tagging then train a classification model to apply to the remaining records)\n\n- Co-occurence/ item sets analysis to find out core ingredients, flavor ingredients, etc. Also, creating an ingredient network so we have an understanding of central nodes (ingredients which are hard to be replaced) and what they are usually being used with. \n\n\n- Complements & Substitution analysis to find how we can switch ingredients for a certain recipe, or can we add in certain extra ingredients. We can try different options such as reading reviews for keyword such as 'I use X instead of Y', 'I subtitute A with B', etc. then build Substitution Networks. Or doing Ingredient Embedding Analysis (maybe using Word2Vec trained on out dataset or something else). Cluster analysis would also be interesting, ingredient in a group are more likely to be used as substitute\n\n- Explore PCA of recipe-ingredient matrix might yield insights on how these ingredients are used together.\n\n...",
      "autoResize": true,
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    },
    {
      "id": "mYJHcHEeh1iuazCnigCRY",
