    {
      "id": "V_SQQxf1h6scjk6FrNjrD",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 8262.691192378765,
      "y": -3409.49832595341,
      "width": 1032.276123046875,
      "height": 657.2919973550574,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#1e1e1e",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 2,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 1,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "index": "b2m",
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 1944347832,
      "version": 5016,
      "versionNonce": 207220680,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": [],
      "updated": 1772502236124,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "- From the review dataset, we have a list of user and their comment. We can\nuse that to create user profile & reference by combining with the recipe data.\nBecause each review have a rating, we can use that to assign an accumulate\npreference score for each ingredient in that recipe, combining over all reviews we\nwill have a good understand of their preferences.\n\n- We can also do the same scoring for other kind of tagging like cuisine, flavor,\ncooking method, nutrient, etc. to have a user score for that.\n-> after that we can combined all those score into a single profile for each user\n\n- Another method might be try building user embedding vectors (user-recipe\nmatrix) then do dimension reduction on them, then visualize those 'concept' from\ndimension reduction to see the trends in the recipes and the users.\n\n- If necessary, do sentiment analysis on reviews. Ratings are fixed-number but\nsometimes high rating can go with negative comment, so understand this can\nhelp use recalibrate the rating so we can make better recommendation, using\nsomething like SentimentIntensityAnalyzer from nltk might be helpful for this\ntask.\n...",
      "fontSize": 26.2916798942023,
      "fontFamily": 5,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": "mYJHcHEeh1iuazCnigCRY",
      "originalText": "- From the review dataset, we have a list of user and their comment. We can use that to create user profile & reference by combining with the recipe data. Because each review have a rating, we can use that to assign an accumulate preference score for each ingredient in that recipe, combining over all reviews we will have a good understand of their preferences.\n\n- We can also do the same scoring for other kind of tagging like cuisine, flavor, cooking method, nutrient, etc. to have a user score for that.\n-> after that we can combined all those score into a single profile for each user\n\n- Another method might be try building user embedding vectors (user-recipe matrix) then do dimension reduction on them, then visualize those 'concept' from dimension reduction to see the trends in the recipes and the users.\n\n- If necessary, do sentiment analysis on reviews. Ratings are fixed-number but sometimes high rating can go with negative comment, so understand this can help use recalibrate the rating so we can make better recommendation, using something like SentimentIntensityAnalyzer from nltk might be helpful for this task.\n...",
      "autoResize": true,
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    },
