    {
      "id": "LI4NRU9CH2V4VWymCvCLJ",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 10656.292124182146,
      "y": -3731.5983854626866,
      "width": 878.8740234375,
      "height": 985.9379960325862,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#1e1e1e",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 2,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 1,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "index": "b37",
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 640793164,
      "version": 7473,
      "versionNonce": 646843848,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": [],
      "updated": 1772502236125,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "- Reinforcement learning model to fill in missing features of review &\nrecipe records.\n\n- For content-based filtering, train TF-IDF model for recipe\ndescription, recipe ingredient list. We can try different TI-IDF\nmodels for comparisions. We can also explore Dense Embeddings and\nother type of deep learning embedding we can use for creating\nrepresentative for similarity calculation \n\n- For collaboration filtering, we use dimension reduction model, such\nas SVD or NMF to create ratings for none-existing user-recipe\nrating pair. We can try other models for this task to have better\ncomparison. Also explore Graph Neural Networks (GNNs) and similar\ngraph based deep learning models that are usually used for\ncollaboration tasks. \n\n- Build goal-based optimization model that will predict a recipe score\nbased on our input goal and the recipe, such as prioritize vegan\nrecipes, healthy recipes, non-spicy, etc.\n\n- Use pretrained food2vec/models to calibrate to our datasets or\ncreating new models and compare with pretrained model for the\ningredient substitution task\n\n- Train sentiment model on review comments to generate sentiment\nscore to be used as adjustment score in recipe ranking\n\n- Explore spelling correction models to fix typo in the user inputs\n\n...",
      "fontSize": 26.2916798942023,
      "fontFamily": 5,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": "93_urEqe7Et3akphEn1B_",
      "originalText": "- Reinforcement learning model to fill in missing features of review & recipe records.\n\n- For content-based filtering, train TF-IDF model for recipe description, recipe ingredient list. We can try different TI-IDF models for comparisions. We can also explore Dense Embeddings and other type of deep learning embedding we can use for creating representative for similarity calculation \n\n- For collaboration filtering, we use dimension reduction model, such as SVD or NMF to create ratings for none-existing user-recipe rating pair. We can try other models for this task to have better comparison. Also explore Graph Neural Networks (GNNs) and similar graph based deep learning models that are usually used for collaboration tasks. \n\n- Build goal-based optimization model that will predict a recipe score based on our input goal and the recipe, such as prioritize vegan recipes, healthy recipes, non-spicy, etc.\n\n- Use pretrained food2vec/models to calibrate to our datasets or creating new models and compare with pretrained model for the ingredient substitution task\n\n- Train sentiment model on review comments to generate sentiment score to be used as adjustment score in recipe ranking\n\n- Explore spelling correction models to fix typo in the user inputs\n\n...",
      "autoResize": true,
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    },
