    },
    {
      "id": "eOJzjJaiLlpp87wCKG99U",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 13464.747553083631,
      "y": -4234.370994325666,
      "width": 1404.4232177734375,
      "height": 1365,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#1e1e1e",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 2,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 1,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "index": "b3N8",
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 189201336,
      "version": 2133,
      "versionNonce": 434345672,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": [],
      "updated": 1772502236125,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "\n- For each recommendation feature, we will create a different tab/page for it. There should be a login\npage so user can log in and use their previous settings and personalized models.\n\n- First page/tab should be a profile page with dropdowns/checkbox which users can confirm their\npreferences. Without any input, we would assume the user have no preferences, and we would only use\ntheir previous reviews to support the recommendation and rankings.\n\nSupport use cases(we will have different filter option/constraints for each use case):\n\n1. Recipe search (using recipe name, recipe description)\n- Input box,  filter dropdowns/checkboxes -> return some recipes that related to the recipe\nname/recipe description with ranking order\n\n2. Image search (recipe images)\n- Upload file button -> classification model -> trying to identify the recipe-> display the recipe\ninformation\n-> ask if user would like to explore or similar recipes\n\n3. Grocery match search\n- Input box to clarify your grocery items -> recommendation options such as using the input ingredient\nonly/using as little extra ingredients as possible, etc. -> find recipes that match the grocery list the\nbest\n\n4. Auto recommendation (using user profiles, popular recipes)\n- Auto create recommendations based on user profiles, previous reviews, and popular recipes in the\ndatabase\n\n---\n\n- We will have an option that allow users to review/rate the recommendations and store it to the\ndatabase, so we can adapt and create better recommendations next time.\n\n- Besides just showing the recommendation names, we will also display their meta info, such as\nnutrient values, calories, ingredient, example picture, healthy score, suggested ingredient switch, etc.\n\n...\n\n",
      "fontSize": 28,
      "fontFamily": 5,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": "z46kv1J3FBslLsCdXUBzP",
      "originalText": "\n- For each recommendation feature, we will create a different tab/page for it. There should be a login page so user can log in and use their previous settings and personalized models.\n\n- First page/tab should be a profile page with dropdowns/checkbox which users can confirm their preferences. Without any input, we would assume the user have no preferences, and we would only use their previous reviews to support the recommendation and rankings.\n\nSupport use cases(we will have different filter option/constraints for each use case):\n\n1. Recipe search (using recipe name, recipe description)\n- Input box,  filter dropdowns/checkboxes -> return some recipes that related to the recipe name/recipe description with ranking order\n\n2. Image search (recipe images)\n- Upload file button -> classification model -> trying to identify the recipe-> display the recipe information\n-> ask if user would like to explore or similar recipes\n\n3. Grocery match search\n- Input box to clarify your grocery items -> recommendation options such as using the input ingredient only/using as little extra ingredients as possible, etc. -> find recipes that match the grocery list the best\n\n4. Auto recommendation (using user profiles, popular recipes)\n- Auto create recommendations based on user profiles, previous reviews, and popular recipes in the database\n\n---\n\n- We will have an option that allow users to review/rate the recommendations and store it to the database, so we can adapt and create better recommendations next time.\n\n- Besides just showing the recommendation names, we will also display their meta info, such as nutrient values, calories, ingredient, example picture, healthy score, suggested ingredient switch, etc.\n\n...\n\n",
      "autoResize": true,
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    },
